{% if emitted.source_kind == 'kpack' %}
{#
   The pinned case list is READ OUT OF the suite template this same run renders, because
   test_packs.cpp.j2 gates cases on has_heuristic, is_multi_pack and behavior_notes and a
   second copy of those conditionals would disagree the moment either grew a case.

   A case the extraction misses -- one whose TEST_F were wrapped across lines -- is left
   out of the pin and reported by the census as registered-but-not-expected: red, not a
   silently narrowed pin.
-#}
{% set packs_source %}{% include 'test_packs.cpp.j2' %}{% endset %}
{% set case_marker = 'TEST_F(Test' ~ config.engine.pascal_name ~ 'Packs, ' %}
{% set expected_cases = [] %}
{% for line in packs_source.split('\n') if line.startswith(case_marker) %}
{% set _ = expected_cases.append(line.split(case_marker)[1].split(')')[0] | trim) %}
{% endfor %}
{#
   The arch restriction is the emitted inventory's own concrete architectures, taken
   from the finalized documents this run wrote. The wildcard key is deliberately not
   among them: "*" is how a descriptor says it ships everywhere, not an architecture a
   shard can be named after, and `ARCHES *` would ask for a shard that never exists.
   The keyword is emitted only when the list is non-empty -- present-with-no-values is
   fatal by contract.
-#}
{% set restricted_arches = [] %}
{% for arch in emitted.arches %}
{% if arch != '*' %}{% set _ = restricted_arches.append(arch) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
## Splice point 5c: P/src/tests/CMakeLists.txt, beside the other per-pack-target
## census calls that follow hkp_verify_embedded_sources(). Add this call:
hkp_register_census_tests(TARGET hip_kernel_provider_census_tests
                          PACK_NAME product
{% if restricted_arches %}
                          ARCHES
{% for arch in restricted_arches %}
                              {{ arch }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
                          SUITES Test{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}Packs
                          EXPECTED_CASES
{% for case in expected_cases %}
                              {{ case }}
{% endfor %}
                          )
##
## `PACK_NAME product` addresses the `product` pack target, wired only where the shipped
## root holds a descriptor AND at least one of them declares an architecture this build
## packs for. A build whose GPU_TARGETS your bundle does not declare leaves production
## packaging dormant: the call registers nothing and says so at STATUS, so leave it
## unguarded.
##
## `ARCHES` narrows registration to the architectures THIS bundle emitted, intersected
## with the arches the pack target was wired for. Without it the suite registers for every
## arch the pack target carries, including ones this bundle ships nothing for, and the
## census then asserts a gfx950 inventory against a gfx942 shard.
##
## Commit your bundle under `E/descriptors/<producer>/<bundle>/` **before** splicing this
## call, or the census runs against a shard without your descriptors.
##
## The call registers one CTest entry per eligible arch:
## hip-kernel-provider-hkp-census-<arch>-Test{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}Packs.
## The EXPECTED_CASES list above is read out of the suite this run rendered; re-splice
## whenever the bundle's shape changes. hkp_register_census_tests() in HkpPackaging.cmake
## documents the keyword contract.
{% else %}
